WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.179 --> 00:00:06.250
♪ ♪

00:00:06.251 --> 00:00:07.418
&gt;&gt; Greg: WASHINGTON, D.C., HAS

00:00:07.419 --> 00:00:10.087
MANY PROBLEMS, MOST HAVE A D OR

00:00:10.088 --> 00:00:11.155
R AFTER THEIR NAMES.

00:00:11.156 --> 00:00:12.790
THANK GOD THE CITIES TACKLING

00:00:12.791 --> 00:00:15.092
THE MOST PRESSING PROBLEM OF AL

00:00:15.093 --> 00:00:16.927
ALL, STRAWS.

00:00:16.928 --> 00:00:19.330
D.C. HAS A PLASTIC STRAW

00:00:19.331 --> 00:00:20.698
INSPECTOR.

00:00:20.699 --> 00:00:22.967
THEY VISIT RESTAURANTS WARNING

00:00:22.968 --> 00:00:25.002
OF FINES IF THEY DON'T GET RID

00:00:25.003 --> 00:00:28.239
OF THE EVIL, THIN HOLLOW TUBES.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:28.906
BEING FOUND WITH A STRAW CAN

00:00:28.907 --> 00:00:30.441
EARN YOU AN $800 FINE.

00:00:30.442 --> 00:00:32.209
THAT'S MORE THAN THE FINE FOR

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:33.911
PRACTICING MEDICINE WITHOUT A

00:00:33.912 --> 00:00:34.512
LICENSE IN CONNECTICUT.

00:00:34.513 --> 00:00:38.816
DON'T ASK ME HOW I KNOW.

00:00:38.817 --> 00:00:39.183
[LAUGHTER]

00:00:39.184 --> 00:00:39.884
WORSE, IT'S MORE BUREAUCRATIC

00:00:39.885 --> 00:00:40.651
HARASSMENT THAT RATTLES CASHIERS

00:00:40.652 --> 00:00:41.719
AND CLERKS JUST TRYING TO DO

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:43.621
THEIR JOBS.

00:00:43.622 --> 00:00:45.189
THE HASSLE SOLVE NO PROBLEMS

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:46.390
WITH THE OVERWHELMING MAJORITY

00:00:46.391 --> 00:00:47.958
OF PLASTIC WASTE IN THE OCEAN,

00:00:47.959 --> 00:00:50.494
WHICH SEEMS TO BE THE HOT-BUTTON

00:00:50.495 --> 00:00:52.296
ISSUE HERE, COMES FROM TEN

00:00:52.297 --> 00:00:54.265
RIVERS, ALL FROM AFRICA AND

00:00:54.266 --> 00:00:55.032
ASIA.

00:00:55.033 --> 00:00:56.467
IT AIN'T US, WHICH POSES A

00:00:56.468 --> 00:00:59.403
PROBLEM FOR LEFT-WING ACTIVISTS

00:00:59.404 --> 00:01:00.171
WHO NEED AMERICA TO PROTEST.

00:01:00.172 --> 00:01:02.440
THE STUFF THAT YOU SEPARATE ENDS

00:01:02.441 --> 00:01:04.642
UP BACK IN THE LANDFILLS BECAUSE

00:01:04.643 --> 00:01:06.043
THERE'S NO MARKET TO SELL THE

00:01:06.044 --> 00:01:06.344
STUFF.

00:01:06.345 --> 00:01:08.879
RECYCLING WAS SOLD TO US AS A

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:10.247
MAGICAL SOLUTION BUT EVEN

00:01:10.248 --> 00:01:11.048
MAINSTREAM MEDIA OUTLETS LIKE 6I

00:01:11.049 --> 00:01:11.082
MAINSTREAM MEDIA OUTLETS LIKE 6U

00:01:11.083 --> 00:01:11.182
MAINSTREAM MEDIA OUTLETS LIKE 6N

00:01:11.183 --> 00:01:11.215
MAINSTREAM MEDIA OUTLETS LIKE 6W

00:01:11.216 --> 00:01:11.248
MAINSTREAM MEDIA OUTLETS LIKE 6I

00:01:11.249 --> 00:01:11.282
MAINSTREAM MEDIA OUTLETS LIKE 6'

00:01:11.283 --> 00:01:12.850
MAINSTREAM MEDIA OUTLETS LIKE 6S

00:01:12.851 --> 00:01:12.883
MAINSTREAM MEDIA OUTLETS LIKE 6G

00:01:12.884 --> 00:01:12.917
MAINSTREAM MEDIA OUTLETS LIKE 6R

00:01:12.918 --> 00:01:12.950
MAINSTREAM MEDIA OUTLETS LIKE 6A

00:01:12.951 --> 00:01:13.417
MAINSTREAM MEDIA OUTLETS LIKE 6E

00:01:13.418 --> 00:01:14.018
MAINSTREAM MEDIA OUTLETS LIKE 6.

00:01:14.019 --> 00:01:16.220
AS USUAL, OUR NATIONS BUSYBODIES

00:01:16.221 --> 00:01:18.022
IGNORE THE CONSEQUENCES OF THEIR

00:01:18.023 --> 00:01:18.356
ACTIONS.

00:01:18.357 --> 00:01:21.092
PLASTIC STRAWS ARE NECESSARY FOR

00:01:21.093 --> 00:01:21.826
PEOPLE WITH DISABILITIES AS WELL

00:01:21.827 --> 00:01:22.660
AS THE ELDERLY.

00:01:22.661 --> 00:01:23.260
BUT WHO CARES.

00:01:23.261 --> 00:01:25.830
EVERY BAND IS CONSIDERED

00:01:25.831 --> 00:01:26.664
PROGRESS FOR FEVERISH.

00:01:26.665 --> 00:01:27.832
EGGS.

00:01:27.833 --> 00:01:30.234
WHY SHOULD SOMEONE, PRODUCTS

00:01:30.235 --> 00:01:32.036
THAT MAKES LIFE EASIER WHEN THE

00:01:32.037 --> 00:01:33.037
LIVES OF ACTIVISTS ARE SO GRIM,

00:01:33.038 --> 00:01:35.573
MORE SO THAN STRAWS, THEY TRULY

00:01:35.574 --> 00:01:39.844
SUCK.

00:01:39.845 --> 00:01:41.879
DANA, 800 BUCKS IN WYOMING,

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:45.750
FLORIDA, MISSISSIPPI.

00:01:45.751 --> 00:01:47.885
SIMPLE ASSAULT AS OF THE FINE

00:01:47.886 --> 00:01:48.419
$500.

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:49.754
&gt;&gt; Dana: HAPPENED TO ME WHEN I

00:01:49.755 --> 00:01:50.454
WAS IN D.C.

00:01:50.455 --> 00:01:51.188
I TRIED TO GET A STRAW.

00:01:51.189 --> 00:01:54.258
I'M KIDDING.

00:01:54.259 --> 00:01:55.693
I DIDN'T GET ANYTHING WITH A

00:01:55.694 --> 00:01:56.227
STRAW.

00:01:56.228 --> 00:01:56.927
I'M GOING NEXT WEEK.

00:01:56.928 --> 00:01:58.229
I WILL CHECK IT OUT.

00:01:58.230 --> 00:02:00.431
THIS REMINDS ME OF WHEN I

00:02:00.432 --> 00:02:01.432
STOCKPILED LIGHT BULBS FOR

00:02:01.433 --> 00:02:01.732
YEARS.

00:02:01.733 --> 00:02:03.667
THERE WAS THE WARNING THAT THE

00:02:03.668 --> 00:02:04.869
LIGHT BULBS WERE GOING AWAY.

00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:09.039
EVERY TIME WE WENT TO -- WHAT

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:10.608
WAS IT, ON CAPITOL HILL IN

00:02:10.609 --> 00:02:11.308
WASHINGTON, D.C., GETS MORE

00:02:11.309 --> 00:02:12.443
LIGHT BULBS.

00:02:12.444 --> 00:02:15.112
THEN WE MOVED THEM FROM D.C. TO

00:02:15.113 --> 00:02:15.479
NEW YORK.

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:16.881
&gt;&gt; Jesse: DID THEY BREAK?

00:02:16.882 --> 00:02:17.314
&gt;&gt; Dana: KNOW.

00:02:17.315 --> 00:02:18.849
BUT I FEEL BAD ABOUT ARE THE

00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:20.818
CLERKS AND CASHIERS GETTING

00:02:20.819 --> 00:02:21.952
YELLED AT BY THE CUSTOMERS.

00:02:21.953 --> 00:02:24.622
THEY WANT A STRAW.

00:02:24.623 --> 00:02:25.256
AND THE FINE.

00:02:25.257 --> 00:02:26.424
BUT THEY DON'T HAVE TO PAY THE

00:02:26.425 --> 00:02:26.724
FINE.

00:02:26.725 --> 00:02:28.392
THE OWNER PAYS THE FINE.

00:02:28.393 --> 00:02:30.127
&gt;&gt; Juan: AS A RESIDENT OF THE

00:02:30.128 --> 00:02:32.096
DISTRICT OF COLUMBIA, YOU CAN

00:02:32.097 --> 00:02:33.230
GET A STRAW, DANA PERINO.

00:02:33.231 --> 00:02:35.166
IT JUST WON'T BE A PLASTIC

00:02:35.167 --> 00:02:35.633
STRAW.

00:02:35.634 --> 00:02:37.435
&gt;&gt; Dana: HAVE YOU TRIED THEM?

00:02:37.436 --> 00:02:39.236
&gt;&gt; Katie: THEY DISSOLVE IN

00:02:39.237 --> 00:02:40.971
YOUR CUP.

00:02:40.972 --> 00:02:41.472
&gt;&gt; Greg: IT'S NOT

00:02:41.473 --> 00:02:42.640
BIODEGRADABLE.

00:02:42.641 --> 00:02:43.841
&gt;&gt; Dana: WE SHOULD HAVE THEM

00:02:43.842 --> 00:02:46.043
ON SET TOMORROW AND START

00:02:46.044 --> 00:02:46.744
"THE FIVE" WITH OUR CUPS WITH

00:02:46.745 --> 00:02:49.380
STRAWS AND SEE HOW LONG THEY

00:02:49.381 --> 00:02:49.680
LAST.

00:02:49.681 --> 00:02:54.819
&gt;&gt; Juan: I CAN SPIT SPITBALLS?

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:55.586
&gt;&gt; Greg: JUAN, THE SPITBALL IS

00:02:55.587 --> 00:02:57.455
THE ISSUE.

00:02:57.456 --> 00:02:59.824
EIGHT GETS SOGGY WITH A PAPER

00:02:59.825 --> 00:03:00.458
STRAW.

00:03:00.459 --> 00:03:02.827
YOU NEED A PLASTIC STRAW FOR

00:03:02.828 --> 00:03:04.361
SPITBALLS AND SOME OTHER THINGS.

00:03:04.362 --> 00:03:06.831
&gt;&gt; Jesse: A DOLLAR BILL, GREG.

00:03:06.832 --> 00:03:10.201
&gt;&gt; Greg: WHAT DO YOU MEAN?

00:03:10.202 --> 00:03:10.568
[LAUGHTER]

00:03:10.569 --> 00:03:13.237
&gt;&gt; Dana: I HAVE NO IDEA WHAT

00:03:13.238 --> 00:03:15.139
YOU'RE TALKING ABOUT.

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:16.640
&gt;&gt; Greg: JESSE, "60 MINUTES."

00:03:16.641 --> 00:03:19.043
IN DECEMBER, THEY DID THIS

00:03:19.044 --> 00:03:19.343
PIECE.

00:03:19.344 --> 00:03:21.078
JOHN TIERNEY, HE HAS WRITTEN

00:03:21.079 --> 00:03:22.046
ABOUT IT.

00:03:22.047 --> 00:03:23.347
JOHN STOSSEL HAS WRITTEN ABOUT

00:03:23.348 --> 00:03:23.848
IT.

00:03:23.849 --> 00:03:25.583
HOW RECYCLING IS MORE EXPENSIVE

00:03:25.584 --> 00:03:26.851
AND NOBODY'S BUYING IT.

00:03:26.852 --> 00:03:28.285
THEY ARE TAKING THE STUFF THAT

00:03:28.286 --> 00:03:29.620
YOU SEPARATE OUT AND THEY JUST

00:03:29.621 --> 00:03:30.754
THROW IT BACK IN LANDFILLS.

00:03:30.755 --> 00:03:33.457
THIS WAS ON "60 MINUTES."

00:03:33.458 --> 00:03:35.292
MAYBE WE ARE COMING TO OUR

00:03:35.293 --> 00:03:36.026
SENSES.

00:03:36.027 --> 00:03:37.361
&gt;&gt; Jesse: I WAS ALWAYS COMING

00:03:37.362 --> 00:03:39.163
TO MY SENSES BECAUSE I NEVER

00:03:39.164 --> 00:03:39.864
RECYCLED EVER.

00:03:39.865 --> 00:03:41.932
EVERYTHING IS COMING BACK FULL

00:03:41.933 --> 00:03:42.399
CIRCLE.

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:44.068
&gt;&gt; Greg: STAY IN THE SAME

00:03:44.069 --> 00:03:44.435
PLACE.

00:03:44.436 --> 00:03:45.736
&gt;&gt; Jesse: THE INSPECTORS JOB

00:03:45.737 --> 00:03:46.036
SUCKS.

00:03:46.037 --> 00:03:48.672
I FEEL BAD FOR THEM.

00:03:48.673 --> 00:03:50.040
DID YOU GET THE JOKE?

00:03:50.041 --> 00:03:51.575
&gt;&gt; Dana: ALREADY USED THAT

00:03:51.576 --> 00:03:51.876
JOKE.

00:03:51.877 --> 00:03:54.678
YOU RECYCLED HIS JOKE.

00:03:54.679 --> 00:03:55.646
&gt;&gt; Jesse: I DO RECYCLE!

00:03:55.647 --> 00:03:57.414
HERE'S MY HONEST OPINION.

00:03:57.415 --> 00:03:59.216
I FLIP-FLOPPED ON THE PLASTIC

00:03:59.217 --> 00:03:59.683
STRAWS.

00:03:59.684 --> 00:04:02.253
I AM ENLIGHTENED.

00:04:02.254 --> 00:04:02.786
JUAN, IT'S POSSIBLE.

00:04:02.787 --> 00:04:03.687
FLIP-FLOPPED BASED ON FACTS.

00:04:03.688 --> 00:04:05.456
IF THEY ARE GETTING IN THE

00:04:05.457 --> 00:04:06.724
POTOMAC BECAUSE THEY CAN BE

00:04:06.725 --> 00:04:08.058
RECYCLED BECAUSE THEY ARE TOO

00:04:08.059 --> 00:04:10.261
SMALL, WHAT'S THE BIG DEAL IF

00:04:10.262 --> 00:04:12.296
YOU USE ANOTHER TYPE OF

00:04:12.297 --> 00:04:12.897
BIODEGRADABLE STRAW?

00:04:12.898 --> 00:04:14.798
OTHER INDUSTRIES CAN POP UP AND

00:04:14.799 --> 00:04:15.499
MAKE THESE THINGS.

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:18.335
IT'S NOT GOING TO CAUSE A HUGE

00:04:18.336 --> 00:04:19.270
DENT IN THE PLASTIC INDUSTRY.

00:04:19.271 --> 00:04:22.039
&gt;&gt; Greg: YOU JUST LOST THE

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:23.641
SPEAKING ENGAGEMENT AT U.S.

00:04:23.642 --> 00:04:24.408
PLASTICS.

00:04:24.409 --> 00:04:25.276
DON'T YOU KNOW.

00:04:25.277 --> 00:04:26.877
THE MORE YOU DEFEND THE STRAWS.

00:04:26.878 --> 00:04:28.679
&gt;&gt; Jesse: THEY PAY WELL.

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:30.047
&gt;&gt; Katie: THERE IS MORE IN THE

00:04:30.048 --> 00:04:32.349
POTOMAC THAN PLASTIC STRAWS.

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:33.083
MUCH BIGGER PROBLEMS.

00:04:33.084 --> 00:04:34.652
THE PROBLEM IS FINDING PEOPLE.

00:04:34.653 --> 00:04:37.254
WE MIGHT HAVE PAPER STRAWS

00:04:37.255 --> 00:04:37.621
TOMORROW.

00:04:37.622 --> 00:04:38.389
I BROUGHT OUR REAL PLASTIC STRAW

00:04:38.390 --> 00:04:39.156
TO SET TODAY.

00:04:39.157 --> 00:04:42.626
I'M WONDERING IF, THE FINE FOR

00:04:42.627 --> 00:04:43.627
HAVING A STRAW IS $800.

00:04:43.628 --> 00:04:46.030
WHAT IS DEFINED FOR SMUGGLING

00:04:46.031 --> 00:04:47.831
STRAWS INTO THE CITY?

00:04:47.832 --> 00:04:51.435
IF I HAVE STRAWS IN MY PURSE.

00:04:51.436 --> 00:04:55.406
IS TEN STRAWS CONSIDERED HIGH

00:04:55.407 --> 00:04:56.840
